WEBVTT

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.360
After World War II, Germany was split 
into two countries, East and West.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.460
The citizens of the two 
nations lived as enemies.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:20.350
In 1967, humanity encountered an alien 
life form on the Moon, the BETA,

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.370
and war broke out.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.690
Six years later, the BETA landed 
in Kashgar, in Central Asia.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.960
<b>Beings of Extra Terrestrial origin 
which is Adversary of human race</b>

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.960
In the midst of the Cold War,

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.150
1983 
East Germany

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.070
humanity was thrust into 
a fight for its very survival.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.280
Frankfurt (Oder)
Approximately 6km West of the Oder River

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:41.100
And ten years later, the war's front lines

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.310
were in the German Democratic 
Republic, East Germany.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.910
The BETA's advance into Europe put 
East Germany in a desperate position,

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.190
and the Ministry for State Security, the Stasi,

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.110
put a surveillance system in place throughout
the country to maintain their fighting forces.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.440
Fear of the state caused the people 
to monitor one another.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.430
The result was a mad society in which parents
blew the whistle on their children,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.560
children on their parents, 
husband on wife, and wife on husband.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.000
We believed in no god, and had 
no one else to believe in.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.450
Our only choices were to die on the 
battlefield, to die in the purges,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.270
or to live like machines.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.000
Even so...

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.660
Even so, I thought to myself that 
I wanted to protect you.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.780
Captain Bernhard, there is a 
request for reinforcements.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.070
I'm refusing it.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.370
We have our own mission.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.240
There they are. The Laser-classes.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.520
They're guarded by Tank-classes.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.400
666th TSF Squadron 
Captain Irisdina Bernhard

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.400
Attention, all units.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.150
666th TSF Squadron 
Lieutenant Walther Kruger

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.150
This is the hunting time you've waited for.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.780
666th TSF Squadron 
Lieutenant Gretel Jeckeln

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:04.470
Squadron 666, of the German Democratic 
Republic, will now begin laserjagd.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.410
666th TSF Squadron 
Lieutenant Pham Thi Lan

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.040
666th TSF Squadron 
Second Lieutenant Anett Hosenfeld

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.030
The forward units will clear a path.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.660
666th TSF Squadron 
Second Lieutenant Sylwia Krzasińska

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.160
Rear units will provide fire support 
and watch our tail.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.420
666th TSF Squadron 
Second Lieutenant Inghild Bronikowski

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.290
Bring down Schwarzesmarken's 
might on those damn BETA!

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.290
666th TSF Squadron 
Second Lieutenant Theodor Eberbach

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:15.650
Roger!

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.140
Open fire!

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.600
All squadrons have begun their advance.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:50.150
The heavy metal clouds will prevent 
further communication.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.730
All four TSF squadrons have now entered combat.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.540
Assault success rate is 66%, huh?

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:01.940
Lieutenant Heisenberg, what's your 
take on the strategic situation?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.050
It depends on the laserjagd's success.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.170
If we want to bring in our air forces,

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.710
we need to take out those Laser-class.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.310
If the BETA advance further, we won't be 
able to maintain our defensive lines.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.440
What squadron will reach the Laser-class first?

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.010
Squadron 666.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:22.950
Walther, you take them.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:23.610
Roger.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.910
Schwarzes-04, how do things look there?

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.540
The Tanks are slowing me down! 
I can't get eyes on the Lasers!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.120
Schwarzes-02. I can't find them, either.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.350
Ammo at 60%.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.790
Schwarzes-05. Ammo at 40% and dropping.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.050
Schwarzes-08. Also at 40%.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:42.880
Anett, calm down!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.410
Die!

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:49.890
Monsters!

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.370
Schwarzes-06, calm down!

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:55.060
I'm just neutralizing the enemies in our path!

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.560
Hey, do something about her.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.320
We're still in the middle of the laserjagd!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.570
This is 07. I'll help 06.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:06.070
Die! Die!

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.820
Anett, please stop!

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.990
You won't be able to avenge 
everyone if you keep this up!

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.270
I...

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:22.500
A-All I can do is kill the BETA...

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.700
The treatment isn't working...

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.230
And every night, I dream about 
everyone who died!

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.850
It's okay. I'll protect you.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:34.410
So calm down.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.380
Okay... Thanks, Inghild.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.390
Insane pilots need to stay off the battlefield.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:40.760
Everything okay now, 07?

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.590
Yes. I'll help 06.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.360
Roger.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.890
Our target's beyond the hill.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:47.760
Let's hurry.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:48.740
Roger.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.080
Schwarzes-08,

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.260
keep an eye on 06 and 07.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.780
Wh-Why me?

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.790
Your response?

00:05:58.840 --> 00:05:59.710
Roger.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.840
Laser-classes sighted.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.130
Here we go.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.840
03 and 04, hit 'em hard.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.780
Kill every last one.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:28.030
I know that, Comrade Captain!

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:46.800
Heavy metal cloud density is dropping.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.360
Monitors are coming back on-line.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.310
That's the 666th Squadron for you.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.560
I can see why they call it 
the Number of the Beast.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:58.940
Major, the laserjagd is a success.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:03.090
Begin area-suppression attacks in 180 seconds.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.220
Order the TSFs to withdraw immediately.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:05.570
Sir!

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:09.900
Get all artillery ready, now!
Order air forces to begin bombing!

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:11.130
All we can do now is pray they come back, huh?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.240
Attention, all units.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.260
Laser-classes have been eliminated.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.370
We will now leave the combat area.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.900
Ascend to an altitude of 100.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.370
Not much time before the artillery hits.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.530
More enemies, Comrade Captain.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.130
Let the infantry handle them, 
and let's get out of here!

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:30.770
More of you? Damn monsters!

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:31.630
Anett!

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.390
I have no time to deal with the mentally ill.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.110
There's no time left!

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.210
Let's get out of here!

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:39.180
But I...

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.660
You need to survive!

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.040
This is stupid.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.200
Why would you bring a lunatic to...

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.580
Inghild!

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:22.600
Lieutenant Pham, Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.690
help me.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.340
I need more people.

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.390
Roger.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.150
There's nothing we can do.

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:42.620
She has twenty minutes at most.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.910
I see. Understood.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.020
Attention, all units.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.210
Second Lieutenant Inghild Bronikowski 
doesn't have long left to live.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:13.250
Thus, I will administer the coup de grâce here.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.810
Wait...

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.480
She's still alive!

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:20.990
I don't want to make her suffer any longer.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.160
B-But...

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.390
There may still be something we can do!

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.500
If we get to base, I'm sure...

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.070
There's nothing we can do.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.210
But...

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.750
Don't worry. I'll do it.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:34.160
Cut your area microphone.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.400
I'll do it in five seconds.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.220
Urgent orders from HQ.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:01.160
A UN TSF unit is requesting aid 
from within Polish territory.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.330
I'm sending two units.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.200
Go make the UN owe us a favor.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:09.020
I'll leave my comrade, the captain, 
to decide who goes.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.850
I'll volunteer.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.830
No, I'll go.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:15.800
You need to take Inghild back to base.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:19.230
The other will be Second Lieutenant Eberbach.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.130
Huh? Me?

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:24.060
Walther will handle Inghild's body.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.010
Let's go.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.060
Roger...

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:35.340
Former Polish People's Republic Territory 
Oder River's Eastern Shore

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.070
I'm not picking anything up.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.480
You're sure the request for 
reinforcements wasn't a bad report?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.030
This is a waste of time.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.780
Second Lieutenant Theodor Eberbach,

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.400
stop being a spoiled brat.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:49.860
Spoiled?

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:51.170
That's right.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:53.180
I'm doing my job!

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.950
Why didn't you help Anett?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.640
Did you think a pilot with 
PTSD was just in the way?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.550
I...

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:04.000
That decision cost Inghild her life.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.750
No matter how good you are,

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:10.130
if you can only protect yourself, 
you don't have the right to be a pilot.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.870
I don't have the right?!

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.880
Are you in any place to say that?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.270
I know what you've done.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:17.650
You're a Stasi—

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.470
You aren't going to finish?

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:24.280
You were going to call me 
a Stasi informant, right?

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.730
If you don't want to be even worse than I am,

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.460
keep your pride as a pilot and fulfill your duty!

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.640
Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.690
I'll handle the BETA.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:52.720
Save the pilot of that TSF!

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.520
Prove to me that you're a pilot!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.290
Damn it!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.450
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.550
L-Lise...

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.110
We're almost to the border.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:36.860
Hang in there!

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:52.870
Daddy!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:55.500
Go, you two!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.580
Theodor, take care of Lise!

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:04.880
Let's go, Lise!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:06.510
But...

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.330
Run! Run!

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.710
Lise!

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:21.820
Brother!

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.610
Lise! Lise!

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:56.430
U-Um...

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:07.110
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.110
Second Lieutenant Katia Waldheim.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:10.700
UN Atlantic Theater First Army,

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.040
German Bundeswehr 101st TSF Battalion.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.760
2nd Company, 3rd Platoon.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:18.460
Fifteen years old.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.770
Born in Hamburg.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.880
Volunteered for the military 
after her parents' deaths.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:25.930
Veteran of multiple battles.

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:30.710
You sure brought us some trouble, didn't you?

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:42.280
U-Um...

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:43.140
Uh...

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.110
Ow...

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:53.290
Um, you're Second Lieutenant 
Theodor Eberbach, right?

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:55.640
Thank you for saving me!

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:57.510
I'm—

00:14:57.510 --> 00:14:58.580
Don't touch me!

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:07.690
I'm sorry.

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:10.090
But I wanted to thank you properly.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:14.890
Do you plan to thank everyone who saves 
you on the battlefield like that?

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:16.350
Yes!

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:20.810
You saved my life, so of course I'd thank you.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:26.900
So did you learn anything new, Comrade Captain?

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:30.570
I was just talking to her about the squadron.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:33.060
She's from the West!

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:35.550
Just what's been publicly broadcast.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:36.120
That's right.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:42.730
East Germany's strongest TSF squadron, 
the 666th, bearing the Number of the Beast,

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.200
AKA the Schwarzesmarken.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.050
You're famous even in West Germany.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:50.760
U-Um, well...

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.300
There's something I need to ask of you!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:57.060
Please let me join your squadron!

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.770
Comrade Captain! What did you tell her?!

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:02.470
Nothing at all.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.070
You can listen to the recording later.

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.280
Second Lieutenant Katia Waldheim,

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.400
would you tell me why?

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:14.070
You know that what you're 
asking is very serious, right?

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:18.390
I've always admired you all.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:21.730
I've always wondered what the 
other Germany was like,

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.430
and who lived there...

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.860
I've always wanted to visit someday.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.460
I've always wanted to make 
friends with East Germans!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.250
Your thoughts, Comrade Lieutenant?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:37.100
You think I, the political commissar, 
would allow it?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.330
She would fill the hole in our ranks.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.520
But still...

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.580
It's a fact that she survived all by herself.

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:46.780
Right, Second Lieutenant Eberbach?

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:52.580
Then you want me to use my authority 
as political commissar?

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.780
I'd like to confirm something, 
Second Lieutenant Katia Waldheim.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:01.240
Yes?

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:05.670
You're seeking asylum in our country, right?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:10.000
And you swear loyalty to your new homeland, 
the party, and the army?

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:13.510
Y-Yes.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:18.510
I, Katia Waldheim, formally request asylum.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:21.760
Very well.

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:24.010
I'll prepare the paperwork.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:26.080
But you're aware that this is a special case,

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:29.900
and not a decision made out of trust, correct?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.650
Yes.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.900
Second Lieutenant Eberbach 
will oversee your training.

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.000
Yes, ma— Huh?

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.980
You saved her.

00:17:37.980 --> 00:17:39.090
Is there a problem?

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:40.630
N-No...

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:44.240
I'm counting on you, Second Lieutenant.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:45.440
Wai—

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:59.490
Theodor, are you mad?

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:02.390
Did I do something wrong?

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:03.850
No.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:06.510
If I've done something wrong, I apologize.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.000
I don't know what to do...

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.380
Don't call me by my first name.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:13.860
And don't treat me as your savior.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.650
I was only following orders.

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.610
That's not true!

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:22.330
You're the first person who ever risked 
their life to save me, Theodor.

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:24.540
Eberbach.

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.220
Huh?

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.180
Oh... I'm sorry!

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.830
Pretend to be friends with someone else.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:30.670
But...

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:34.630
I want to know more about you, Eberbach!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:38.490
I'm from the West and you're from the East,

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:41.220
but I'm sure that we can get along!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:44.710
If East and West work together, 
we can even beat the BETA!

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:45.890
Come with me!

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:50.380
Eberbach!

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.200
So that's the new girl?

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.360
Second Lieutenant Eberbach...

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.410
What are you...

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.010
What's wrong, Theodor—

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.360
Listen to me!

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:17.060
Your words mean nothing in this country.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:20.550
If they heard you, the Stasi 
would arrest and kill you!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.000
The enemy isn't just the BETA.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.900
The humans next to you are your enemies, too!

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:28.810
Humans are my enemies?

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:31.740
There are Stasi informants everywhere.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:34.170
They show no mercy to traitors.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.400
Don't give them any opportunities.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.820
That goes for the rest of the squadron, too.

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:40.700
So...

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:45.160
Don't trust Captain Irisdina Bernhard.

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.560
She sold out her own brother to 
the Stasi to become a GDR hero.

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.710
There is no freedom in this country!

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:56.880
That's the truth of the 
country you wanted to see!

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.610
The truth of the East Germany 
you always admired!

00:19:59.610 --> 00:20:00.720
Got it?

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:06.180
Enough. I'm going back inside.

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:14.230
What are you doing?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.470
Theodor,

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:29.570
I'm here for a reason.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.380
A reason?

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:32.510
What is it?

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.500
Do you know a man named Lieutenant 
General Alfred Strachwitz?

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:41.840
I'm here...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.140
I'm here to look for him.

00:22:22.170 --> 00:22:28.200
Somewhere in the German 
Democratic Republic

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:34.260
I told you everything... Everything!

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:35.110
So...

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:38.830
Everything?

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:42.460
You shouldn't lie to me.

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:45.220
I'm not lying! I—

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:55.710
We already know all about your plan

00:22:55.710 --> 00:22:59.980
to secretly work with the West 
to cause division in the East.

00:23:00.340 --> 00:23:02.510
You are enemies of the state.

00:23:02.510 --> 00:23:03.820
More than the BETA.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.670
Enemies of the state?!

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:07.030
That's the Stasi!

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:10.280
You're trying to turn East Germany 
into your own private—

00:23:11.230 --> 00:23:17.040
East Germany must unite to fight the BETA.

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:20.150
Thus, we will lead the nation.

00:23:20.680 --> 00:23:24.790
For East Germany... No, for Europe and the world.

00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:27.260
We will bring death to those in our way.

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:29.220
Do it.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:31.800
Strafe.

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:42.560
Good grief.

00:23:46.610 --> 00:23:48.940
It's been a long day for both of us.

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:51.020
Indeed. I hate days like this.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:55.500
<b>To Be Continued</b>
